{"id":"ashdoth-pisgah","name":"Ashdoth-Pisgah","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:ashdoth-pisgah"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Ashdoth-pisgah","text":"(Deut. 3:17; Josh. 12:3; 13:20) in Authorized Version, but in Revised Version translated “slopes of Pisgah.” In Deut. 4:49 it is translated in the Authorized Version “springs of Pisgah.” The name Ashdoth is translated “springs” in the Authorized Version, but “slopes” in the Revised Version, of Josh. 10:40 and 12:8. It has been identified with the springs under Mount Nebo, now called ‘Ayun Musa."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H798","lemma":"אַשְׁדּוֹת הַפִּסְגָּה","xlit":"ʼAshdôwth hap-Piçgâh","gloss":"Ashdoth-Pisgah, a place east of the Jordan","kjv":"Ashdoth-pisgah","count":3,"share":0.75},{"strong":"H6160","lemma":"עֲרָבָה","xlit":"ʻărâbâh","gloss":"a desert","kjv":"Arabah, champaign, desert, evening","count":3,"share":0.75},{"strong":"H4217","lemma":"מִזְרָח","xlit":"mizrâch","gloss":"sunrise","kjv":"east, rising","count":3,"share":0.75},{"strong":"H1020","lemma":"בֵּית הַיְשִׁימוֹת","xlit":"Bêyth ha-Yshîy-môwth","gloss":"Beth-ha-Jeshimoth, a town East of the Jordan","kjv":"Beth-jeshimoth","count":2,"share":0.5},{"strong":"H3672","lemma":"כִּנְּרוֹת","xlit":"Kinnᵉrôwth","gloss":"Kinneroth or Kinnereth, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Chinnereth, Chinneroth, Cinneroth","count":2,"share":0.5},{"strong":"H4417","lemma":"מֶלַח","xlit":"melach","gloss":"powder","kjv":"salt","count":2,"share":0.5}],"verses":["Deut.3.17","Josh.12.3","Josh.13.20","Deut.4.49"],"related":[{"id":"pisgah","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.143,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"beth-jeshimoth","type":"lexical","strong":"H798","why":"both lead with אַשְׁדּוֹת הַפִּסְגָּה (H798)"},{"id":"desert","type":"lexical","strong":"H6160","why":"both lead with עֲרָבָה (H6160)"},{"id":"deserts","type":"lexical","strong":"H6160","why":"both lead with עֲרָבָה (H6160)"}],"works":[]}
